+\paragraph{Arithmetic--geometric location.}
+The tower $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_{F_n}[1/p]$ consists
+of finite etale covers of $U_p=\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z[1/p]$.
+At each layer, the Hilbert class group describes abelian
+$p$-power torsors over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_{F_n}$;
+the principal $p$-prime imposes complete splitting there.
+Their norm limit is the actual integral module $X$ in (QI.1).
+The character specialization in (QI.4) is the dual of the strict
+negative Tate-sheaf extension group in (FW.2), with precisely
+the twist $-e$.  The carried integral VK-PT comparison (FW.1)
+therefore identifies that specialized compact group with
+$K_{2e}(\mathbf Z)\{p\}$, or equivalently with the relevant
+$H^2_{\acute et}(U_p,\mathbf Z_p(e+1))$.
+This retains the finite arithmetic obstruction; no passage to
+rational mixed Tate motives or to a characteristic ideal
+removes it.  These are the existing integral comparison inputs,
+not a new theorem about an integral category of motives.
 
